From c173b6006e4fa8b4785ef5c2132e82d7c5869ef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:24:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 849/913] plat-stm32mp1: add trace in
 stm32mp1_get_lp_soc_mode()

For PSCI_SYSTEM_SUPSPEND request, when Standby is limited by OP-TEE
(so without the power domain based on SMC), it is difficult to
understood the cause of the issue without modifying the code.

This patch allows to have the minimal information in console needed to
understood this restriction, when the console is not suspended by Linux
kernel during system suspend request with:

echo N > /sys/module/printk/parameters/console_suspend

By default the console is suspended in suspend mode and the trace is
not displayed and the added latency for trace is acceptable for this
use case (vs time to freeze linux tasks).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 8e99a91c36ca2ba1f198588d67d934c39f71f382 plat-stm32mp1: add trace in stm32mp1_get_lp_soc_mode()]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I1eb3337354ec377b27ddd3f03f8c188e81c66941
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/610145
Reviewed-by: Valentin CARON <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/power_config.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/power_config.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/power_config.c
index 377379ca6..f99227042 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/power_config.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/power_config.c
@@ -335,6 +335,18 @@ uint32_t stm32mp1_get_lp_soc_mode(void)
 	    !stm32mp1_lp_soc_mode_is_supported(mode))
 		mode = STM32_PM_CSLEEP_RUN;
 
+#ifndef CFG_STM32_LOWPOWER_SIP
+	/* Trace to debug low power mode restriction (no Standby) */
+	if (mode != STM32_PM_CSTANDBY_ALLOW_STANDBY_DDR_SR) {
+		IMSG("EXTI C1IMR1=%x C1IMR2=%x C1IMR3=%x\n",
+		     exti_read_imr(0), exti_read_imr(1), exti_read_imr(2));
+		IMSG("mode=%x for power domain: CORE=%d CORE_RET=%d\n",
+		     mode,
+		     get_pm_domain_state(STM32MP1_PD_CORE),
+		     get_pm_domain_state(STM32MP1_PD_CORE_RET));
+	}
+#endif
+
 	return mode;
 }
 
